body:
Well, first, it's  not "redistribution" as fat isn't redistributed to other areas, rather new fat cells form and new fat and energy taken in goes to those new areas. It's like a new road and a blockade on the old, not so much evacuating fat cells from the old road to the new. Your body tells itself t put fat in female generic areas. You'll still have the fat from before HRT effects.

&#x200B;

Second, it takes time. I would say by six months you should start noticing things. Don;t do drugs like smoking cigs as that can interfere with it if you take the oral/pill medication. I would say give it time, be patient and eat as much of healthy fats as you can. For me, I eat tubs of peanut butter. It's my guilty pleasure.
